1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,610
If you shattered your wrist,

2
00:00:01,650 --> 00:00:03,890
imagine gluing the bones back together.

3
00:00:03,930 --> 00:00:05,750
Researchers actually did it.

4
00:00:05,790 --> 00:00:07,450
They developed an experimental glue

5
00:00:07,490 --> 00:00:09,980
inspired by oysters sticking to rocks.

6
00:00:10,020 --> 00:00:11,440
It grips bone even inside

7
00:00:11,480 --> 00:00:13,120
a wet, bloody wound.

8
00:00:13,160 --> 00:00:14,730
In one reported wrist case,

9
00:00:14,770 --> 00:00:16,450
surgeons secured the broken pieces

10
00:00:16,490 --> 00:00:18,130
in just three minutes.

11
00:00:18,170 --> 00:00:20,270
The fracture still needed months to heal.

12
00:00:20,310 --> 00:00:21,750
But as new bone grows,

13
00:00:21,790 --> 00:00:23,790
the glue gradually disappears.

14
00:00:23,830 --> 00:00:24,890
Your body replaces

15
00:00:24,930 --> 00:00:26,610
the stuff holding you together.

